# The Phase 3 exit map.
#
# The plan's exit criterion for this phase names four things: a parametric lift,
# a scripted-discrete mover, a crusher, and a rail -- with anchored riding
# predicting cleanly in BOTH motion modes. This map is that criterion, made of
# geometry, so the claim is tested rather than asserted.
#
#   sector 0   the yard: where a player lands, and where the rails are
#   sector 1   a parametric lift. Rises 3 units on a fixed schedule, so a client
#              computes its position for any tick from parameters sent once.
#   sector 2   a scripted-discrete mover. Drifts on a schedule with no closed
#              form, so its offset is streamed every snapshot and a rider falls
#              back to anchor-relative prediction (design §3.2.5).
#   sector 3   a crusher: its CEILING descends, which is the only way the gap a
#              body occupies can close.
#
#   y
#   ^   +--------+--------+
#   |   |   2    |   3    |   discrete mover | crusher
#   |   +--------+--------+
#   |   |   0    |   1    |   yard | parametric lift
#   |   +--------+--------+
#   +-------------------------> x
#
# Both movers rest FLUSH with the yard. A lift whose resting floor is above
# STEP_HEIGHT cannot be walked onto -- correctly, since that is what the step
# rule is for -- so a platform a player is meant to board has to be level with
# the ground at the bottom of its travel.

sector floor 0 ceil 12 tag 1
  vertex  0   0   wall
  vertex 20   0   neighbor 1
  vertex 20  20   neighbor 2
  vertex  0  20   wall
end

# tag 100+N: a parametric lift rising N units.
sector floor 0 ceil 12 tag 103
  vertex 20   0   wall
  vertex 40   0   wall
  vertex 40  20   neighbor 3
  vertex 20  20   neighbor 0
end

# tag 400+N: a scripted-discrete mover with N units of range. No path is
# declared because there is none to declare -- that is what makes it the mode a
# client cannot predict.
sector floor 0 ceil 12 tag 402
  vertex  0  20   neighbor 0
  vertex 20  20   neighbor 3
  vertex 20  40   wall
  vertex  0  40   wall
end

# tag 200+N: a crusher whose ceiling drops N units. Ceiling 12 minus 11 leaves a
# gap of 1 -- half a standing body.
sector floor 0 ceil 12 tag 211
  vertex 20  20   neighbor 1
  vertex 40  20   wall
  vertex 40  40   wall
  vertex 20  40   neighbor 2
end

spawn yard      10 10 0
spawn lift      30 10 0
spawn drifter   10 30 0
spawn crusher   30 30 0

# A rail across the yard, and a wire bolted to the discrete mover so that a rail
# on an unpredictable platform is exercised too -- the waypoints ride it exactly
# as a rail on a lift rides that.
rail tag 1
  waypoint  2  2 1
  waypoint 18  2 1
  waypoint 18 18 1
end

wire tag 2
  waypoint  2 22 6
  waypoint 18 22 6
end

junction 0 2 to 1 0
